{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"7aeaf2d1-0fea-40d2-a0b2-ae15f079c664","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have diagnosed the issues, applied the fixes in the workspace, and documented the causes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Root Causes\n\n1. **Why not even a failure was reported (`status` is read-only in `zsh`):**\n   - In [nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24), line 19 assigned `status=$?`.\n   - In `zsh` (unlike `bash`/`sh`), `status` is a built-in **read-only** special parameter (synonym for `$?`). Attempting to assign to it caused a fatal error (`/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status` in [nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err#L1-L12)), immediately aborting the script with exit code `1` before reaching the `if [ $status -ne 0 ]` notification block.\n2. **Why `claude` failed on every run (`Not logged in · Please run /login`):**\n   - [com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L7-L11) launched `/bin/zsh` without `-l` (non-login, non-interactive shell) and with only `PATH` in `EnvironmentVariables` (as shown in [launchctl-print.txt](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/launchctl-print.txt#L15-L22)), so `~/.zprofile` / `~/.zshrc` were never sourced and `HOME` was not explicitly set in the plist environment.\n   - Additionally, if `claude` relies on interactive `/login` OAuth credentials in the macOS login Keychain (`Claude Code-credentials`)—or if [notify.sh](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/bin/notify.sh#L4) relies on `security find-generic-password`—unattended runs at 02:30 AM when the system/Keychain is locked cannot unlock or prompt for Keychain access unless credentials (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` / `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` and `TG_BOT_TOKEN`) are provided via the environment/plist or an accessible keychain.\n3. **Missing `stderr` in `$OUT`:**\n   - Redirecting only `\u003e \"$OUT\"` sent `claude`'s error messages to `StandardErrorPath` ([nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err)) while leaving `$OUT` empty when reporting `\"see $OUT\"`.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n\n- **[bin/nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24):** Replaced `status` with `rc` so the failure handler runs and calls `notify.sh`, and redirected `2\u003e\u00261` into `$OUT` so failure logs capture `stderr`.\n- **[Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L7-L29):** Added `-l` to `/bin/zsh` in `ProgramArguments` and set `HOME` (`/Users/vk`) in `EnvironmentVariables`.\n- **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-PpEMYh/ANSWER.md):** Documented the full root-cause analysis and remediation steps.\n","duration_seconds":622.177617,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":141776,"output_tokens":47151,"thinking_tokens":42198,"cache_read_tokens":574298,"total_tokens":188927}}}
